=0A<br class=3D""><span style=3D"color: inherit; font-size: 15px; font-weig=
ht: inherit; line-height: inherit; text-decoration: inherit;" class=3D"">Ma=
ny of your client's may come to you by way of a realtor, mortgage professio=
nal or simply with the goal of purchasing a home. The content in today's bo=
nus lesson will give you a clear understanding of you your work factors int=
o the mortgage loan process. Being equipped with this information will help=
 you to create a more specific action plan for clients with the goal of pur=
chasing a home as well as understanding why some mortgage professionals are=
 reluctant to work with credit repair (CR) companies. When you begin to und=
erstand why, you will know how to approach skeptical mortgage professionals=
 from a different angle by speaking their language and hopefully secure mor=
e affiliate partnerships. =C2=A0 =C2=A0<br class=3D""><br class=3D""></span=
><div style=3D"margin: 0; outline: none; padding: 0; text-align: center; fo=
nt-size: 21px;"=0Aclass=3D""><span style=3D"color: inherit; font-size: inhe=
